- majority/plurality/tied/unanimous classification replaces the earlier blanket "50%" framing
- entropy/support-size/max-probability explicitly flagged as near-redundant under n=3, one
  primary measure preferred
- majority-vs-vector section strengthened with 3 real, concrete examples
- distribution-similarity vs. framing-effect-similarity kept conceptually distinct (never
  "accuracy")
- PRIMARY/SECONDARY/EXPLORATORY labeling introduced
- language audited for overclaiming ("best", "genuinely", "clearly", etc.)

Run: python build_notebook_1.py
Then: jupyter nbconvert --to notebook --execute --inplace <output path>
"""
